2026-10-23T18:41Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/worktree-exit-preflight.sh:76` gates `/roar`'s worktree removal
(`skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh:411`) on `git status --porcelain
--untracked-files=all`, which does not list ignored files. In a repo whose
`.gitignore` is `*` (this harness), any file outside the allow-list (a
draft, notes, a generated report) reads as clean and `git worktree remove`
deletes it with the tree. PR 1640 met the same blind spot in
`worktree-gc.sh` and fixed it there with `ownerless_tree_clean`
(`--ignored=matching`, caches and `.tmp/` tolerated). Found by the roar
sweep after PRs 1638/1640 (journal 2026-10-23-worktree-gc-ownerless-locks-1638-1640).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The exit preflight blocks removal on an ignored file other than
      regenerable caches, the root `.venv/` and `.tmp/` (its own gate).
- [ ] One shared helper serves `worktree-gc.sh` and the preflight, or the
      two lists are pinned equal by a test.
- [ ] A test under a `*` ignore rule: an ignored draft blocks removal; a
      tree holding only caches passes.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
